// The War Council — yuddha kanda, Lanka
// Source: Valmiki, Yuddha Kanda, sargas 6-19 (verify)
// Migrated from the old script format. Not yet staged for the Ramlila stage.

>> scene lankaCourt style=kachni
>> music lanka
>> cast ravana at 0.3 pose=sit y=-70
>> cast minister at 0.5 face=left
>> cast kumbhakarna at 0.92 face=left scale=0.5
>> cast vibhishana at 0.64 face=left
>> cast indrajit at 0.76 face=left
>> prop throne throne at 0.3
>> title Meanwhile, in Lanka / The War Council
Lanka still smells of smoke. One monkey did that. Ravana calls his council.
MINISTER: You conquered the gods, lord. What is a man, and some apes? Give the word, and we will eat them on the far shore.
KUMBHAKARNA: You should have asked us before you took her, not after. It was badly done. But it is done, and you are my brother. I will kill them for you.
VIBHISHANA: There have been omens since she came. Cows give no milk. The fires will not catch. Brother, give her back. It is not weakness to return what was never yours.
>> heads \{"voices":\["king","honour","pride","anger"\],"lines":\{"king":"l3.7","honour":"l3.8","pride":"l3.9","anger":"l3.10"\}\}
INDRAJIT: My uncle is the one coward born in our house. I bound Indra himself. Shall I fear two men?
>> pose ravana point
RAVANA: A kinsman is glad when his kinsman falls. If anyone else had said this, he would be dead. Get out of my sight.
>> pose vibhishana namaste
VIBHISHANA: You are my elder, and I spoke for your good. Pleasant counsellors are easy to find. Guard yourself, and Lanka. I am going.
>> move vibhishana to 0.64 in 1.2 y=-260 keepface
>> exit vibhishana to right y=-300
He rises into the air with four companions, and crosses the sea.
>> scene camp clear
>> enter rama:exile from left to 0.3 in 0.1 colour=true
>> enter sugriva from left to 0.16 in 0.1 colour=true
>> enter vibhishana from right to 0.66 in 1.4 colour=true
>> pose vibhishana namaste
SUGRIVA: Ravana's brother, arriving on the eve of war. He is a spy. Kill him.
RAMA: He has come asking for shelter. If Ravana himself came and said "I am yours", I would not turn him away. It is my vow.
>> pose rama give
>> sound bell
He sends for sea water and, there on the sand, crowns Vibhishana king of a city that has not yet fallen.
-> END
